  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "tooth extraction",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "tooth extraction; pulling a tooth",
      "explanation": "The dental procedure of removing a tooth from its socket in the jawbone."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21278_basshi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{親知|おやし}らずを{抜歯|ばっし}した。",
      "english": "I had my wisdom tooth extracted.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21278_basshi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{抜歯|ばっし}の{後|あと}は{激|はげ}しい{運動|うんどう}を{避|さ}けてください。",
      "english": "Please avoid intense exercise after a tooth extraction.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21278_basshi_ex3",
      "japanese": "{虫歯|むしば}がひどくなり、{抜歯|ばっし}しか{選択肢|せんたくし}がなくなった。",
      "english": "The cavity got so bad that extraction was the only option left.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {抜|ばつ} (to pull out, to extract) and {歯|し} (tooth). A standard dental term widely understood by non-specialists. Note the reading: {歯|し} uses the on'yomi, not the kun'yomi {歯|は}. The homophone {抜糸|ばっし} (removal of stitches) is a completely different word.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {抜歯|ばっし}する: to extract a tooth\n- {親知|おやし}らずの{抜歯|ばっし}: wisdom tooth extraction\n- {抜歯後|ばっしご}: after tooth extraction\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {親知|おやし}らず: wisdom tooth — the tooth most commonly associated with {抜歯|ばっし}\n- {虫歯|むしば}: cavity, tooth decay — a common reason for extraction\n- {歯科|しか}: dentistry — the field of medicine dealing with teeth\n- {抜糸|ばっし}: removal of stitches — a homophone with a completely different meaning",
